  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Africa Economic Transformation Advocacy</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A 2-day round-table dialogue in Addis Ababa that brings together a group of around 15-20 Africa-based thought leaders (including researchers, activists, NGOS &amp; farmer organisations) to discuss economic transformation in the context of the SDG&#x2019;s. The aim of such an event would be (1) sharing CAFOD and partners&#x2019; current research &amp; thinking with other thought-leaders &amp; key institutions to contribute towards influencing in-country economic development processes (2) networking &amp; building relationships with thought-leaders with the aim of developing joint messaging &amp; influencing strategies (3) Strengthening CAFOD &amp; partner expertise around economic development issues &amp; explore the possibility of strategies for joint-influencing &amp; work &amp; (4) To consolidate CAFOD&#x2019;s position on this topic through information sharing with our partners &amp; other thought leaders. This event would be followed by an extra 2-3 days with CAFOD partners to develop further thinking &amp; options for joint-work.</narrative>
  </description>
